        "y_pct": 50.0
      },
      "cmf": {
        "material": "PC-ABS",
        "finish": "textured_heavy",
        "color": "Safety orange (RAL 2003) body with dark graphite (RAL 7021) grip band and bumper pods",
        "secondary_ops": [
          "tpe_overmold",
          "pad_print",
          "laser_etch"
        ]
      },
      "intent_anchors": [
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA1",
          "statement": "Keep the four raised bumper pods as the first contact points on every face so drop energy is absorbed away from the display bezel and seal line.",
          "category": "durability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA2",
          "statement": "Preserve the deep lateral grip ribs and stepped waist overmould; they must remain usable with 3 mm-thick work gloves and wet hands.",
          "category": "usability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA3",
          "statement": "Maintain the front intake as a discrete field below the display with ePTFE membrane behind it; do not merge it into the display bezel or reduce its open area.",
          "category": "durability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA4",
          "statement": "Keep the safety-orange high-visibility body colour and dark contrast band; do not shift to low-saturation or metallic finishes.",
          "category": "cmf",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA5",
          "statement": "Retain PC-ABS for the shells and overmoulded TPE for the grip band to meet impact and UV targets within the cost ceiling.",
          "category": "cost",
          "must_preserve": true
        }
      ],
      "rationale": "The bumpered silhouette answers the brief's durability priority directly: raised corner pods act as sacrificial crash structures, letting the thin 125 x 75 x 30 mm shell stay light (about 78 g of plastic leaves ample margin under 180 g) while still surviving 1.5 m drops. The front-face layout is deliberately asymmetric in hierarchy: display high and centred for quick glance reads, intake low and wide so the ePTFE membrane and gasket sit away from impact zones and splash paths, and the USB port moved to the bottom face so the gasketed door is protected by the body when the unit is laid down. Textured-heavy PC-ABS with TPE overmould gives the grip and UV stability the site environment demands; cost is held by using two shells plus one overmould instead of a separate bumper assembly, keeping the BOM within the CNY 18 ceiling while accepting the ~CNY 2.7 vent cost noted in the contract conflict."
    },
